White plays rook a3,

01:10:51.160 --> 01:10:52.440
Black has no moves,

01:10:52.440 --> 01:10:57.400
Again, let's say the black just continues accumulating on the king side, bang,

01:10:57.400 --> 01:11:04.980
Knight g7, king g7, and now a very common follow-up is to play either knight h2 and

01:11:04.980 --> 01:11:10.400
open up the pathway for the queen, or just drive the queen up to h6 with a completely

01:11:10.400 --> 01:11:12.000
decisive attack,

01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:13.480
Check,

01:11:13.480 --> 01:11:17.380
Let's say that the king tries to run to the center,

01:11:17.380 --> 01:11:19.560
We just go knight g5, check,

01:11:19.560 --> 01:11:23.640
We take back with the bishop, and it's very obvious where this is going and not in a favorable

